                {
                    "file": ".clang-tidy",
                    "line": 278,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Lets have that discussion on discord at some point.  std::source_location is kind of an annoying case where it by design needs to defeat this check.\n(example)\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/ac2ff47405b7ae136f10a6407c3c63b666a384dc/http/logging.hpp#L103\n\nwhich isn't great that we have a rule that we MUST bypass for the normal expected std usage.  FWIW, I was also trying to boil out all the company specific checks for the reference to avoid objections, but I could see us making an exception for this one.\n\n\nI don't have a super strong opinion either way until something breaks."
                }
            ],
